The '''1976 African Cup of Nations''' was the tenth edition of the [[Africa Cup of Nations]], the [[association football]] championship of Africa ([[Confederation of African Football|CAF]]). It was hosted by Ethiopia. The format of competition changed from [[1974 Africa Cup of Nations|1974]]: the field of eight teams was still split into two groups of four, but a final stage was introduced with the top two finishers of each of the first stage groups, in the form of a semi-final and a final. This is the same approach that was followed in the 1974 and 1978 World Cups. [[Morocco national football team|Morocco]] won its first championship by topping the final group. [[Guinea national football team|Guinea]] finished second.

Until Kenya, Tanzania and Uganda won a joint bid to host the 2027 edition of the tournament, it was the last one to be held in East Africa.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/clyg0j1l4dqo|title=Afcon 2027: When is the next Africa Cup of Nations tournament?|last=Chowdhury|first=Tasnim|date=20 January 2026|website=BBC Sport|access-date=19 March 2026}}</ref>

